  "domain": "ai",
  "definition": "Fairness in machine learning is the study and practice of ensuring that learned models do not produce systematically disadvantageous outcomes for individuals or groups defined by protected attributes such as race, gender, or age. It encompasses formal fairness criteria \u2014 including demographic parity, equalised odds, and individual fairness \u2014 and the techniques used to measure and mitigate disparate impact before, during, or after training. The field is central to responsible and ethical AI, balancing accuracy with equitable treatment.",
